import{_ as i,o as t,c as n,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 916 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 15 — Observe First, Then Limited Intervention","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 916 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 15 — Observe First, Then Limited Intervention","no":916,"module":5,"tags":["Charter","Article 15","Observe First","Limited Intervention","Causal Threshold"],"related":["83-Observe-First-Limited-Intervention Guideline","84-Archaeology Agreement General Outline","89-Time-Paradox Prevention Mechanism"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0916_模块5-第十五条-先观测后有限干涉.md","filePath":"en/0916_模块5-第十五条-先观测后有限干涉.md"}'),r={name:"en/0916_模块5-第十五条-先观测后有限干涉.md"};function o(s,e,l,h,c,u){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="entry-916-myriad-rank-republican-civilizational-charter-·-article-15-—-observe-first-then-limited-intervention" tabindex="-1">Entry 916 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 15 — Observe First, Then Limited Intervention <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-916-myriad-rank-republican-civilizational-charter-·-article-15-—-observe-first-then-limited-intervention" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 916 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 15 — Observe First, Then Limited Intervention&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 5 · Civilization Final-Finalization Canonical Entries | Benchmark base: Documents 83, 84, 89</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-observe-without-touching-measure-without-disturbing" tabindex="-1">Introduction: observe without touching, measure without disturbing <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-observe-without-touching-measure-without-disturbing" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: observe without touching, measure without disturbing&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Article 14 governs &quot;whether you may go&quot;; Article 15 governs &quot;what to do after going.&quot; It writes the Observe-First-Limited-Intervention Guideline (Document 83) directly into the charter: observe without touching, measure without disturbing, examine before moving, move with measure. For an unfamiliar plane or a historical period, Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s strong ones may only watch first; only after watching, understanding, and assessing, may they make a limited move. This is not timidity, but the deepest awe for the causal law.</p><p>This article is from beginning to end placed under the six top-level axioms — the anti-predation axiom draws the bottom line, the republican axiom of Myriad Races establishes the subject, the collective-ascension axiom sets the direction, the causal self-discipline axiom guards the boundary, the law-first axiom preserves self-consistency; the five together constitute this article&#39;s insurmountable spiritual boundary.</p><p>Together with the previous five axioms, this article is also bound by Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing and layabouts retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose more and higher levels of infinity; predation thus fundamentally loses meaning.</p><h2 id="i-jurisprudential-basis" tabindex="-1">I. Jurisprudential Basis <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-jurisprudential-basis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Jurisprudential Basis&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This article is based on the Observe-First-Limited-Intervention Guideline (Document 83), the Archaeology Agreement General Outline (Document 84), and the Time-Paradox Prevention Mechanism (Document 89). Its jurisprudence is cognitive humility: even plane-sovereign strong ones cannot fully master all causal associations of one time node or one plane civilization. Direct intervention may trigger unpredictable chain reactions; full observation is the only reliable means to minimize risk. The causal self-discipline axiom is here concretized into an operational process.</p><h2 id="ii-normative-content-hard-indicators-for-observation-and-intervention" tabindex="-1">II. Normative Content: Hard Indicators for Observation and Intervention <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-normative-content-hard-indicators-for-observation-and-intervention" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Normative Content: Hard Indicators for Observation and Intervention&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Article 15 quantifies the process into hard indicators:</p><ol><li><strong>Observation duration</strong>: no less than 1% of the target period, and no less than 72 hours of the home plane&#39;s standard time;</li><li><strong>Observation dimensions</strong>: matter, energy, life, consciousness, causality five dimensions, none dispensable;</li><li><strong>Observation neutrality</strong>: pure passive perception, no communication, no traces, no hints, no thought waves released;</li><li><strong>Intervention scope</strong>: no more than 1% of the permitted area;</li><li><strong>Intervention degree</strong>: bound by intervention threshold (area total energy × causal-sensitivity coefficient × 1/10000);</li><li><strong>Intervention time</strong>: no more than 10% of observation duration, and no more than 24 hours.</li></ol><h2 id="iii-scope" tabindex="-1">III. Scope <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-scope" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Scope&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This article applies to all cross-plane expeditions, time retrogression, archaeology, and diplomatic operations. The higher the civilization level and the more critical the historical node, the higher the causal-sensitivity coefficient, the lower the intervention threshold — at critical nodes almost no substantial energy injection is allowed. This article applies equally to plane-sovereign strong ones and ordinary cultivators; thresholds are not relaxed because the strong are bold.</p><h2 id="iv-consequences-of-violation" tabindex="-1">IV. Consequences of Violation <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-consequences-of-violation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Consequences of Violation&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Intervening with insufficient observation, missing a dimension, disturbing the target during observation, breaking through intervention scope or threshold, overstaying in the target period, all constitute unconstitutionality under this article. Consequences: immediately suspend and forcibly withdraw; the causal deviation already caused starts a correction procedure, and the operator bears correction costs; those triggering time forks or cyclical-harvest-type disturbances are pursued heavily under Article 4 and historical-reversal prevention.</p><h2 id="v-supervision-mechanism" tabindex="-1">V. Supervision Mechanism <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-supervision-mechanism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Supervision Mechanism&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This article is executed by Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision: observation duration, five-dimensional coverage, and intervention thresholds are automatically verified by anchor anchoring devices; intervention-permitted area and energy output are real-time compared; all operations are recorded in the time-operation archive library for permanent preservation; the Time-Law Committee independently inspects anomalous intervention behavior.</p><h2 id="vi-a-pair-of-eyes-that-watched-for-72-hours" tabindex="-1">VI. A Pair of Eyes That Watched for 72 Hours <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-a-pair-of-eyes-that-watched-for-72-hours" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. A Pair of Eyes That Watched for 72 Hours&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Article 15&#39;s most patient picture is a pair of eyes that watched for 72 hours. The observer is required, in pure passive state, to watch a target period&#39;s matter, energy, life, consciousness, causality five dimensions for the full minimum duration. Others may feel this is too long and too slow, but precisely these 72 hours let him avoid later filling a precipitancy pit with countless expensive causal corrections. Observing first is not hesitation, but compressing the cost of ignorance to the minimum. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s strong ones thus develop a peculiar humility: the longer they watch, the more they know they should not rush to act; the clearer they see, the more they understand that even acting must act with restraint.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><p><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: full advance observation avoids expensive post-hoc causal correction; it is the most cost-effective energy saving</p></li><li><p><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: random intervention and rewriting other planes&#39; history is essentially predation on their causality; this article positively prohibits it</p></li><li><p><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo-type protagonists break into other worlds and freely rewrite plot; Heng Yuan Zhou five-dimensional observation, threshold constraints, time-limited withdrawal</p></li><li><p><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: what is protected is all beings in all unfamiliar planes and all historical periods</p></li><li><p><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: the observe-intervene closed loop lets civilization infinitely explore more unknown planes without collapsing</p></li><li><p><strong>Universal equal infinity</strong>: every being inherently possesses basic infinite power; the easygoing layabouts retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose higher-level infinity; predation thus fundamentally loses meaning</p></li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Observe first, limited intervention is Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s mature posture for exploring the cosmos. It tells Myriad Ranks: curiosity is no sin, but curiosity with humility deserves the infinite cosmos. First understand the world, then talk about changing the world.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/83-先观测后有限干涉准则.html">Entry 83 · Observe-First-Limited-Intervention Guideline</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/84-考古协议总纲.html">Entry 84 · Archaeology Agreement General Outline</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/89-时间悖论防控机制.html">Entry 89 · Time-Paradox Prevention Mechanism</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/905_模块5-第四条-因果自律原则.html">Entry 905 · Article 4 Causal Self-Discipline Principle</a></li></ul>',25)])])}const p=i(r,[["render",o]]);export{m as __pageData,p as default};
